# services/api/.dockerignore
#
# The root .dockerignore does NOT apply to this image. Docker reads
# <context>/.dockerignore, and this service is built with `build: ./services/api`
# (compose) or `docker build ./services/api`, so the context root is this
# directory. Without this file the build context included services/api/.venv —
# a host-built virtualenv of several hundred megabytes, wrong architecture,
# uploaded to the daemon on every build.
#
# SECURITY, not tidiness: the .env rules exist because anything in the build
# context can be baked into a layer, and layers stay readable through
# `docker history` and `docker save` even if a later layer deletes the file.
# Secrets are injected at run time only.

.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

tests
docs
*.md
railway.json
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
